      {
        "review_id": 205141006,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r205141006-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Other Worldly",
        "text": "It is hard to describe this place, relaxing, sad, confronting? It will leave a lasting impression on you. Witnessing cremations and death so publicly is very alien from the way we deal with it in the west. For many this may be the first time you have seen dead bodies and it feels wrong to be taking photos and watching families experiencing grief. It is almost like a factory. Smoke wafts up from multiple funeral pyres. It takes 3hrs to burn a body and they get through 30 a day. The charred remains are just pushed into the river. There is the spiritual aspect too, gold robes, offerings etc - the whole place is drenched in traditions. The Sadhu's are great characters too. They will pose with you for photos for 10 or 15Rs. Spend some time here just to soak in the atmosphere, have respect for the mourners and don't be too intrusive.",
